---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
---
<LegalLayout title="Terms of Use" description="Website use, quotation enquiries, technical files and the scope of manufacturing information published by Belaro Precision.">
  <h2>1. Website purpose</h2>
  <p>Belaro Precision is the brand used on this website by {site.legalName} (<span lang="zh-CN">{site.legalNameZh}</span>), based in {site.location}.</p>
  <p>This website introduces Belaro Precision’s CNC machining and coordinated secondary-process support for industrial OEM projects. These terms concern use of the website. They do not replace a written quotation, purchase order acceptance, confidentiality agreement or manufacturing contract agreed for a particular project.</p>
  <h2>2. Capability information</h2>
  <p>Service descriptions, materials, tolerances and application examples provide general guidance. Suitability, achievable tolerances, inspection records, treatment specifications and delivery depend on the actual drawing, geometry, material and agreed production scope. Illustrations explain component types and do not establish customer relationships or an inventory of standard products.</p>
  <p>Grinding, heat treatment, surface finishing and other secondary processes may be coordinated through suppliers. The applicable process route and responsibilities must be agreed for each project.</p>
  <h2>3. Enquiries and quotations</h2>
  <p>Sending a form or receiving an acknowledgement does not create an accepted manufacturing order or a guaranteed price or delivery commitment. Quotations require review of the supplied requirements. Price, currency, payment, shipping, taxes, acceptance criteria and delivery terms are to be confirmed in the applicable written commercial documents.</p>
  <h2>4. Drawings and submitted material</h2>
  <p>Only submit files you are authorised to share. Identify the current drawing revision, critical requirements and any handling restrictions. Do not upload unlawful content, malicious files or controlled information without first agreeing an appropriate handling route.</p>
  <p>Submitting an enquiry does not transfer ownership of your drawings to Belaro Precision. The form does not itself establish a separate non-disclosure agreement. Agree any required confidentiality arrangements before submitting sensitive files. Information handling is described in our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>5. Orders, changes and concerns</h2>
  <p>The website does not offer online checkout or take payment. Cancellation, changes, returns, rework and refund arrangements for custom-manufactured parts are addressed in the applicable written order terms and subject to applicable law. If a supplied part raises a concern, contact us with the order reference, drawing revision and supporting details for review.</p>
  <h2>6. Appropriate use and website content</h2>
  <p>Do not interfere with the website, attempt unauthorised access or misuse the enquiry service. Website branding, text and design are protected by applicable intellectual property rights. Third-party materials remain subject to their owners’ rights. Obtain permission before using content beyond what applicable law permits.</p>
  <h2>7. External links and availability</h2>
  <p>External websites have their own terms and privacy practices. Links are provided for information. Website content may be updated and access may occasionally be interrupted. Contact us to confirm any information that is material to a purchasing decision.</p>
  <h2>8. Contact and updates</h2>
  <p>For website questions, project requirements or order concerns, use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Changes to these website terms will be published here with an updated date. Nothing in these terms excludes rights that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p>
</LegalLayout>
